Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.710 align:start position:0%
 
hello everyone and  thank you for joining this session  focused on making business calls safer  and more effective with verified calls  my name is gal i'm a product manager at  google  and i'm joined by my teammate steve who  leads our partnerships  let me kick things off by sharing a  personal story  last month my band tried to call me  several times  about the potential fraudulent activity  on my account  but to be honest i just missed those  polls in the sea  of spam courses that i received every  day  i only realized that something was wrong  after a week when i tried to use my  credit card and it declined  now luckily i had a spirit card so no  a big damage was done but you can  imagine how stressful this situation  might have been  with slightly different circumstances  and  this story puts the spotlight on  the importance of effective  communication  over the phone between businesses and  consumers  so today i'll start off by sharing a  pain point we identified  in in those communications and now we  went  about developing a solution around it  and then i'll turn it to stephen  who will explain how we work with  leading partners  in order to solve this huge pain points  to as many users and  as many businesses as we can  when we look at the data we see that the  average person receives 30 spam calls  each month  and over 2019 there was a sizable  increase in phone calls  the vast majority of businesses feel  outbound calls are important for them to  meet their customer service goals  but here's the problem like me  most consumers simply don't answer their  phone if they don't recognize the number  so there's a massive gap in the  perceived importance  of polls and their actual effectiveness  which is low because people don't answer  so how do we reach this stage  today any device that is connected to  the internet  is capable of making voice calls through  voip  this means that the good old color id  system which displays the caller party  number  can be spoofed very easily there's no  trust in the system  so in practice the person that sits in  the other side of the world  can make a call to my phone and it will  look like  a similar as a call for my local a  bank number so why would consumers trust  uh phone calls anymore  this brings us to verified goals being  helpful and provide  a trust experiences to our users is that  correct what we do at google  and on the left of the screen you can  see our business call  looks today at best it's an unidentified  call  nothing personal it's just a phone  number it doesn't mean  anything to the user and it looks very  similar to  a spam call i receive or the bank call i  missed they look exactly the stem  next you'll see how a verified calls  look like  [Music]  so let's walk through the experience on  the top we got a blue badge  with a verified check mark and we also  display the name and logo of the brand  so the user can know who's calling  finally  we allow the user to state the reason  for calling  and think just think about how wonderful  would have it been if my band could show  hey  this is me calling and this is the  reason about a potential fault in your  account  i will obviously pick this phone call up  in a second  and as you can see we included all of  the information that consumers value in  order to make sure we set the ground up  for an engaging and productive  communication between the two  sides so  we call this product verified calls  so i want to let walk you through what  verified means  for one it signals that the business has  passed google's verification process  it also validates that the call is  coming from  a the number is shown in other words  it's not spoofed  and finally give the user the  information they need including the  reason for calling  so they can make an informed decision  let me walk you through the verification  process we use an  out-of-band channel to verify the calls  meaning that the phone call it still  goes through regular channels without  any change  and the verification is done separately  through an api  and to make it even easier for brands to  join we work with selected telephony  providers to integrate the api  and perform the verification and this  minimize the friction  for brands to join the first step is to  query  the api for reachability data and make  sure the phone number  can deliver a verified course experience  once this is done the next step is to  send google the brand phone number the  consumer phone number  and the call reason and google syncs  this information with the device  and once the voice call arrives the user  will see  the verified calls ui and now  i'm excited to share with you our demo  which you can see how easy it is to get  your calls verified  to verify a call the first step is to  check if the phone number is reachable  as you can see i received a response  that the  device is indeed reachable so i can  continue to the next step and send the  verified calls information  since i received the 200 response from  the server i know  my data was received and i can go ahead  and make a regular phone call  and the phone call will be verified  [Music]  without going into too many details i'll  just say that  our services are powered by the great  infrastructure of google cloud  and i will end my section by mentioning  that  we have designed this api with our  user's privacy in mind  and google removes any personal  information after the verification  is complete now i'm happy to turn this  over to steve that will show you how we  found  how we are partnering with businesses  and share the tremendous interest we  think  thanks gal as you recall from the  beginning of the presentation  87 of consumers don't answer calls from  unknown numbers  this is particularly a problem for  urgent calls like gao's case with this  bank  by verifying the caller with logo and  other details like call reason  our research shows we can make calls  more trustworthy  communicate the relevance to the user  and ultimately improve answer  for the launch of verify calls google  has partnered with leading providers  like the ones on this page  to make calls more trustworthy and  relevant for consumers  for the latest on all partners  supporting verified calls  please visit the website below  our focus on making business and  consumer communications more trustworthy  and engaging doesn't stop at voice calls  back in december 2019 we publicly  launched verified sms  similar to how verify calls enhances  calling experiences  verified sms makes business sms  messaging safer and more trustworthy  by adding sender verification and  branding  many brands like 1 800 flowers  kayak and google pay are already sending  messages with verified sms which is live  across nine countries  including us and canada and north  america brazil and mexico and south  america  uk spain and france and europe  and india and the philippines in asia  and we have more countries planned in  2020 for more information on this  service  please visit the link below  when we started down this path of  creating both verified sms and verified  calls we expected verified  communications to be valuable to both  businesses  and users in a recent user cinema survey  in the us and in brazil for verified sms  we tested this assumption and the  feedback was overwhelmingly positive  in that same survey we were both  positively surprised  to see how strong user sentiment was  across  the customer life cycle particularly  areas  that influence new and repeat business  like business consideration likelihood  to purchase  and likelihood to recommend while we  haven't conducted the same user  sentiment survey for verified calls  given how new it is  anecdotal evidence from partner  discussions give us confidence that  sentiment will be equally strong for the  service too  verified calls is first available in  these five countries  us mexico and brazil and the americas  spain and europe  and india and asia with more countries  planned in 2020  the google phone app and verify calls  comes pre-loaded  on many android devices in these markets  including ones from  motorola nokia xiaomi  one plus and of course pixel however if  you don't already have the google phone  app on your android phone that's okay  coming soon you'll be able to download  it from the play store  for partners and businesses wanting to  take advantage of verified calls  it's simple to get started just register  your interest  in the website or email us directly for  more information  thank you for joining galanite today to  hear how verified calls  makes business calls safer and more  purposeful have a great day

